WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.700
Russia tonight,

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.302
breaking the nuclear arms control

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:04.004
treaty with the United States

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.005
for the first time

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:05.772
since the signing

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.907
of the transformational New START treaty.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:08.942
Russia is refusing

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.076
to allow the US

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.045
to inspect its nuclear weapons.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.380
Now, this move comes at a moment

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.147
where the world faces

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.149
a higher highest risk of nuclear conflict

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.250
since the Cold War.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.451
And it is happening is Putin

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.819
and his military leaders

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.889
have threatened nuclear war,

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:25.325
although with regard

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:28.561
to the threat of a nuclear war.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:35.068
--- you are right...

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.603
The threat is growing.

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.671
So why hide the truth?

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.140
If we don't have the resources

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.076
to defeat the Naito Block

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.478
with conventional means,

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.880
we get to work not.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.149
But we have nuclear weapons for that.

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:49.582
So

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.819
there's more where that came from.

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.421
I mean, even two weeks ago,

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.589
Putin's top ally and Russia's former

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:57.357
president, Dmitry

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.525
Medvedev, warned quote,

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:00.126
The loss of a nuclear power

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.428
in a conventional war

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:02.729
can provoke the outbreak

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.364
of a nuclear war.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:05.231
Putin's breaking

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:06.266
the most significant arms

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.634
treaty in modern history comes

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.602
as his back is up against the wall.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.671
I want you to just listen to this

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.672
from Russian state media.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.007
This is a well-known and highly

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.208
respected Russian analyst

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:17.977
both chancellor.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:18.244
I believe

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.380
that by the start of the mobilization,

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.048
our airborne forces lost

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:24.217
40 to 50% of the staff,

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.420
40 to 50% just coming out

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.589
and saying that gone, dead.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:30.690
And Western officials today

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.191
warn that Putin

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:32.659
does not have the manpower

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:34.594
to replace all of them

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:36.663
or the more than 100,000 Russians

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:37.897
who are estimated to have already died

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.165
on the battlefield.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:39.666
And Putin's

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.401
reliance on the Wagner group to fight

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:42.435
is also now running,

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.037
it appears, up against its own

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.171
manpower issues.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:45.872
They're now apparently

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:46.639
looking for prisoners

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.041
from Ukrainian prisons.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:48.942
So these are Ukrainians

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.443
who have been spending months in prison

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.444
in a war zone,

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:52.612
now being recruited to come out

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:53.580
and kill Ukrainians.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.881
For Wagner Group,

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.216
the mayor of little poll today

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.183
saying that Wagner fighters

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.651
are being sent to a little pole,

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.252
to a little pole

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.720
to look for future bargaining rights

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.655
among their prisoners.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:03.623
Now, the Wagner group is trying

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:04.591
to turn this weakness

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:04.924
into a way

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.092
to mock the United States

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.360
saying that it welcomes American

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.896
fighters to the group as a press unit.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.131
And in a statement to CNN,

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:11.998
they wrote this

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.066
We would like to inform you

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.234
that if American citizens

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.668
wish to join the bargaining group,

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:16.069
they can

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.070
then send their appeal

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.872
to the Wagner press service.

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.907
We will definitely look into it.

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:21.107
All right.

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:21.574
In a moment,

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.275
you're going to hear more

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:23.109
from the front lines

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.111
about the state of Putin's Wagner group,

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:26.980
which is so crucial to all of this,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.381
including why the Ukrainians say

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.949
Wagner's fighters often

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.784
seem like they're on drugs.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:32.752
We begin tonight with Fred

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.487
Pleitgen on the ground in Ukraine near

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:35.288
where some of the worst

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.557
fighting has been raging in back moot.

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:37.891
And Fred,

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.325
I know you've had a chance to be there

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:39.926
on the front line.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.694
You've spoken to Ukrainian troops

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.263
who are fighting the brutal

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.697
Wagner soldiers.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:45.565
What are they telling you?

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:48.868
Higher and well,

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:49.769
they tell us that the going

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:50.803
there is extremely tough

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.071
and it's extremely difficult for them

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.873
to hold the line precisely

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.408
because of what you were just saying,

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:57.010
because the Wagner group

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.711
has such a high rate of attrition.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.213
They saw so many bodies

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.047
at these frontline

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:02.782
trenches that the Ukrainians are in.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:03.783
It's really difficult

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:04.951
to defend these trenches.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.885
And just when the Ukrainians

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:06.653
think they're done,

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:08.922
the next wave of Wagner fighters come.

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:10.790
Now, of course, the attrition rate

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:11.658
among those Wagner

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.293
fighters is extremely high.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.627
Many of them get killed.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.563
But as we know for Yevgeny

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.997
Prigozhin, the head of Wagner,

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.832
all of these people are expendable.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.201
Now, we did manage to speak

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.435
to some Ukrainian troops

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:23.469
who fight Wagner

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.938
virtually every day,

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.506
who witnessed this every day.

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:27.373
And here's what they told us

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:33.213
going

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:34.080
underground with

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.348
Ukraine's frontline

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.150
defenders against Russia's brutal

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.718
private military company,

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.620
the Wagner Group.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:43.590
Andre and Boris say they battled Wagner

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.725
stormtroopers nearly every day.

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:48.695
God, this is what it was like

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:50.063
when a handful of their troops

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.364
were attacked

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:53.866
by about 200 Wagner

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:54.634
fighters.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:59.172
Who were fighting

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:02.108
for about 10 hours in a row.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.577
And it wasn't like just waves.

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.913
It was uninterruptedly.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.881
So it was just like

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.217
they didn't stop coming

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:14.120
Andrei says his men took out scores

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.922
of Wagner soldiers

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:17.957
until they themselves had to retreat.

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:21.794
140 of them, 80 were wounded

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.896
and 60 were killed.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:27.567
And my platoon was 13 people,

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.570
plus several from infantry.

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:34.140
It was about 20 soldiers from our side

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:35.541
and

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:38.544
no, let's say 200 from their side.

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:40.013
Wagner's tactics,

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:40.647
he says

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:41.080
they try

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.048
to overwhelm

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:42.882
the Ukrainians

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.951
by sending waves of fighters,

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.252
many of them convicts,

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:48.221
recruited straight out of jail.

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:51.624
They make the group, let's say, from ten

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:55.662
soldiers is passing 30 meters.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:57.897
Then they started digging in

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:59.632
and keeping the position.

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:01.801
The next group is coming next.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:02.468
30 meters

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:05.471
they reach their position and the going

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:05.872
next.

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:08.141
30 meters also digging.

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:09.008
And that's

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:10.576
how step by step

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:12.645
they're trying to move forward.

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:15.281
The Ukrainian say Wagner fighters often

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.482
seem drugged.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:17.450
The machine gunner

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.218
was almost getting crazy

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:21.354
because he was shooting at them.

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:21.754
And he said,

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:24.190
I know I shot him, but he doesn't fall.

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:27.260
And then after some time when he maybe

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:29.495
bleeds it out already.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.464
So he just only falls down.

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:35.601
It looks like it's very, very likely

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:38.071
that they are getting some drugs

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.439
before attack.

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:41.207
The unit provided us with a recording

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:42.675
they say is of André

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:45.278
questioning a captured Wagner fighter.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:49.349
He got the phone off of the nozzle

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.718
that was spheroids

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:55.555
inside their glass.

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:56.456
So there's more to cover.

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:57.824
There's lots of

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:04.697
pressure to caution us

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:07.300
Yes.

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:11.070
We reached out to Wagner's boss, Yevgeny

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.106
Prigozhin, about allegations of abuse

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:14.140
in their ranks.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.842
This was his answer on Wagner's

00:06:15.842 --> 00:06:17.710
social media account.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.312
Dear CNN, he writes.

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:21.180
Do you really think that we will discuss

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.815
our military issues with you

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:24.517
while you are an open enemy?

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:25.918
It's the same as discussing

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:26.786
military matters

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:28.921
and sharing information with the CIA.

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:30.423
Andre says no matter

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:31.691
how many more fighters

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:33.192
Prigozhin throws at them,

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:34.861
they will resist

00:06:34.861 --> 00:06:36.963
This is the war for freedom.

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:39.532
It's a war for democracy.

00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:41.234
Yes, it's not even for me.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.935
It's not even the war between

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:44.237
Ukraine and Russia.

00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:47.140
Well, this is a war between a regime

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:49.475
and, uh, democracy.

00:06:52.512 --> 00:06:54.280
So some pretty strong words there, Erin.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:54.714
And certainly

00:06:54.714 --> 00:06:56.582
one of the things that we did get from

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:57.183
those soldiers

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:58.618
is that the morale is still pretty high.

00:06:58.618 --> 00:06:59.919
And they say that they're themselves

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:00.753
are pretty surprised

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:01.087
at how

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:03.122
well they are actually still be able

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:04.123
to hold the line,

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:05.758
despite the fact that the Russians

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:07.326
are throwing so many bodies

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:08.194
at all of this.

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:08.761
And right now,

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:09.262
for them,

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:10.730
it's getting even more difficult

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:11.197
because of course,

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:12.532
we know that Yevgeny Prigozhin,

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:13.433
the Ukrainians say,

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:15.601
really wants to give Vladimir Putin

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.003
a win there in Bermuda.

00:07:17.003 --> 00:07:18.871
However, the Russian military

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:20.673
also wants to give Vladimir Putin a win.

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:20.840
That's

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:21.507
why there's many

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:23.042
Russian regular military

00:07:23.042 --> 00:07:24.577
units out there as well right now.

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:26.045
So the Ukrainians really fighting

00:07:26.045 --> 00:07:29.115
two very, very strong forces in that area

00:07:29.115 --> 00:07:30.483
and trying to hold on Erin.

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:32.452
Fred Pleitgen, thank you so much.

00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:33.653
Incredible reporting there,

00:07:33.653 --> 00:07:34.620
hearing that soldier.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.389
I want to go now to Crystal

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:38.124
Groves of the executive director and lead

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:39.992
Russia investigator for Bellingcat

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:41.561
His work was the core of the Oscar

00:07:41.561 --> 00:07:43.296
nominated documentary Navalny,

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:43.896
where you can watch

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:44.764
Christo tracked down

00:07:44.764 --> 00:07:45.331
Putin's man

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:46.899
who poisoned the Russian opposition

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:48.267
leader, Alexei Navalny.

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:50.369
Christo also recently was put on

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:52.004
Russia's most wanted list.

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:53.139
And so I want to start with Fred's

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:54.273
reporting on the partner group.

00:07:54.273 --> 00:07:55.741
There's a lot there.

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:56.175
Let's start

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:57.310
with what we heard that soldiers

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.412
saying to Fred, talking about

00:07:59.412 --> 00:08:00.413
Wagner prisoners

00:08:00.413 --> 00:08:01.814
and prisoners and fighters,

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:03.783
many of whom are prisoners. Right.

00:08:03.783 --> 00:08:04.650
Fighting in March

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.385
and appearing to be on drugs.

00:08:06.385 --> 00:08:06.586
Well,

00:08:06.586 --> 00:08:08.588
we have to be careful with statements

00:08:08.588 --> 00:08:08.955
like this.

00:08:08.955 --> 00:08:10.823
Because it's kind of the oldest

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:12.391
trope in warfare

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:13.626
that people assume

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:15.561
that the other side is on drugs.

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:16.696
We've heard this back

00:08:16.696 --> 00:08:17.497
in the Second World War.

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:18.130
We fought back to

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:18.831
the beginning of the war

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:20.266
when the Russians were accusing

00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:20.733
the brave

00:08:20.733 --> 00:08:21.901
Ukrainians of being on drugs,

00:08:21.901 --> 00:08:22.602
because otherwise

00:08:22.602 --> 00:08:24.770
they can't be so brave in advance so,

00:08:24.804 --> 00:08:26.105
so quickly.

00:08:26.239 --> 00:08:27.907
So I don't know that that is a fact.

00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:29.108
But could it be a fact?

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:30.042
I would say yes,

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:32.011
because Prigozhin has an obsession

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:34.614
with chemical weapons, with poisons.

00:08:34.614 --> 00:08:35.381
He actually

00:08:35.381 --> 00:08:35.948
his phone

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:37.450
number is in the coal

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:39.085
records of the lead jeer

00:08:39.085 --> 00:08:40.353
you military intelligence

00:08:40.353 --> 00:08:42.922
poison doctor of the of the Russian army.

00:08:43.189 --> 00:08:44.524
They exchange information.

00:08:44.524 --> 00:08:45.191
There have been

00:08:45.191 --> 00:08:46.092
previous allegations

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:47.527
that precautions has poisoned

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:49.128
journalists as well.

00:08:49.128 --> 00:08:50.296
And we know that this unit

00:08:50.296 --> 00:08:51.130
that he communicates

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.298
with actually does develop

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:53.933
advanced medications,

00:08:53.933 --> 00:08:55.234
let's call it this way

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:57.003
for pain relief of soldiers

00:08:57.003 --> 00:08:58.905
and any of these could have side effects

00:08:58.905 --> 00:09:00.873
or the main effect of actually

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:02.041
putting a soldier

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:03.976
in a sort of a drowsy state. Right.

00:09:03.976 --> 00:09:05.912
So when you say whether it's true or not,

00:09:05.912 --> 00:09:07.013
certainly there's enough data points

00:09:07.013 --> 00:09:08.347
to indicate it certainly could be

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:10.049
and all of that.

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:11.551
So when you hear Fred,

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:12.184
also talking about

00:09:12.184 --> 00:09:13.052
these waves of fighters,

00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:15.154
the soldier talks about 200 of Wagner

00:09:15.588 --> 00:09:17.757
to about 20 Ukrainians.

00:09:17.924 --> 00:09:18.758
So we hear about those

00:09:18.758 --> 00:09:19.592
overwhelming numbers.

00:09:19.592 --> 00:09:20.660
At the same time, we're hearing that

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.361
he's running out of soldiers.

00:09:22.361 --> 00:09:23.863
Wagner, he's having trouble recruiting,

00:09:23.863 --> 00:09:24.597
trying to find

00:09:24.597 --> 00:09:26.165
maybe even Ukrainian prisoners.

00:09:26.165 --> 00:09:28.668
How stable is promotions power right now?

00:09:29.268 --> 00:09:30.336
Well, what we're seeing

00:09:30.336 --> 00:09:32.004
is a competitive market.

00:09:32.004 --> 00:09:33.539
We have the army competing

00:09:33.539 --> 00:09:34.307
against promotion

00:09:34.307 --> 00:09:35.508
because it could be competing

00:09:35.508 --> 00:09:37.143
against the army

00:09:37.243 --> 00:09:39.545
that's both a political competition

00:09:39.545 --> 00:09:40.146
because Prigozhin

00:09:40.146 --> 00:09:41.347
wants to get a political role.

00:09:41.347 --> 00:09:43.082
We've discussed this on this show,

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:44.684
and he's slowly progressing to actually

00:09:44.684 --> 00:09:46.652
being recognized as a political

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:49.155
almost a sovereign entity within Russia.

00:09:49.155 --> 00:09:49.989
One example of this

00:09:49.989 --> 00:09:51.090
is that only yesterday

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.558
the Russian Ministry of Defense

00:09:52.558 --> 00:09:53.526
finally promised

00:09:53.526 --> 00:09:54.126
that it will start

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:55.428
providing heavy equipment

00:09:55.428 --> 00:09:57.430
to so-called volunteer units.

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:58.664
And he's he's not

00:09:58.664 --> 00:10:00.333
the PMC is a volunteer unit.

00:10:00.333 --> 00:10:01.834
So they're recognizing

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:03.169
this is one of one of them.

00:10:03.169 --> 00:10:04.437
So he's achieving that.

00:10:04.437 --> 00:10:05.671
And therefore,

00:10:05.671 --> 00:10:06.472
I can say that

00:10:06.472 --> 00:10:07.673
the Ministry of Defense

00:10:07.673 --> 00:10:09.075
is losing in this political battle.

